; claude: what a planetarium computes (apps/education/): where a star
; is in a place's sky at an instant (Celestial: sidereal time,
; precession, altitude and azimuth), where the Sun, the Moon and the
; planets are (Ephemeris: Kepler's ellipses, the Moon's disturbances),
; the bright stars and the constellations' figures (Bright_stars), and
; the sphere drawn flat (Stereographic). Used by TinyStellarium; the
; seasons, the phases and the tides of the education apps to come
; would share it.
;
; Pure OCaml, no gui, no playground: in the package tiny_appkits, as
; tiny_appkits.appkit_astronomy, so every backend, the web one
; included, can use it.
(library
 (name appkit_astronomy)
 (public_name tiny_appkits.appkit_astronomy)
 (wrapped false)
)
